# Development Workflow

## Use npm scripts only

Run tasks through the `package.json` scripts - never `npx`, global installs, or direct tool binaries. Custom scripts are fine.

- `npm run lint` - oxlint (use `npm run lint:fix` to autofix)
- `npm run make` - docs + types (`make-types` then `make-docs`)
- `npm run make-docs` / `npm run make-types` - run individually when iterating
- `npm test` - ava under `NODE_ENV=test` (starts/stops the test server via pre/post hooks)

## Node version & native modules

- Use `nvm use` to pick up the version in `.nvmrc`.
- `better-sqlite3` is a native module locked to the Node ABI it was compiled against. If you see
  `ERR_DLOPEN_FAILED` or a `NODE_MODULE_VERSION`/ABI mismatch, the active Node doesn't match the
  build. Fix it by rebuilding:

```bash
npm rebuild better-sqlite3
```

Note: `.nvmrc` and the version `better-sqlite3` was built against can drift apart - make them agree.

## JSDoc must be jsdoc2md-safe

`npm run make-docs` uses jsdoc2md (catharsis), which rejects TypeScript-only type syntax. Keep types
in a form both TypeScript (checkJs) and catharsis accept:

```js
// ❌ Breaks jsdoc2md: arrow-function types and inline optional (?:) object props
// @param {(text: string, i: number) => string} build
// @type {(...args: unknown[]) => void}
// @type {{ embedding?: number[] }}

// ✅ Use @callback for function types
/**
 * @callback PromptBuilder
 * @param {string} text
 * @param {number} index
 * @returns {string}
 */

// ✅ Then reference the named callback from @type casts
let debug = /** @type {PromptBuilder} */ ((text, index) => `${index}: ${text}`);

// ✅ Use @typedef + optional [prop] for object shapes
/**
 * @typedef {object} EmbedResponse
 * @property {number[]} [embedding]
 */
```

Always add JSDoc (with `@param`/`@returns`/`@typedef`) to exported functions and class members.
Never use TypeScript-only function syntax in any JSDoc tag or cast, including inline `@type`
annotations. If a function value needs a type, define a named `@callback` and cast to that name.

## oxlint

The `no-unsafe-*` rules are warn-level and fire at untyped boundaries (SQLite rows, `fetch`/SDK
JSON, markdown-it tokens). Fix them in `src` with a named `@typedef`/`@callback` plus a targeted
cast (`const data = /** @type {EmbedResponse} */ (await response.json());`), and type caught errors
as `const error = /** @type {Error} */ (err);`. These rules are intentionally disabled for tests.
